                    layout_fail "st_read_single_block's disassembly holds no instruction materializing 43605 = **0xAA55** [hit=$mbr_sig_hit bytes=${#blk43_body} addr=$blk43_addr next=$blk43_next], the MBR signature rung 48's derived cell \`_rd_mbr\` compares against. An MBR ends with \`0x55 0xAA\` at bytes 510-511, which is little-endian word 127's HIGH half, so the cell is \`(w[127] >> 16) & 0xFFFF == 0xAA55\`. Zero here is either the arm not publishing the cell at all or a body that claimed the comparison without making it - both leave the press unable to tell an MBR from a sector that merely happens to be 512 bytes long"
