                    mi_switch_txt="that keeps the exec alive on the HFS arm (892): the strategy serves the VOLUME there, so mockfs must map the Mach-O from MEMORY"
                    mi_why="**892: ON THE HFS ARM IT MUST BE ONE.** \`STAGE90_XNU_HFS_ROOT_MEDIA=1\` moves \`st_medium_disk_base(0)\` to the volume (\`g_stage90_root_hfs\`), so a \`mi_mdev = 0\` here would send mockfs's file node through \`st_media_strategy\` and hand process 1 the VOLUME's raw bytes - \`0x482B\` where \`MH_MAGIC\` must be - and \`load_init_program\` fails \`/sbin/launchd\` with ENOEXEC, which is the rung-61 press (892 section 4). The flag must follow the switch"
                else
                    mi_expect=0
                    mi_switch_txt="rung 60's own (the strategy already serves the Mach-O, so the memory-backed branch is declined)"
                    mi_why="**Rung 60 IS that word being ZERO**: mockfs takes the memory-backed branch on it, so a body whose first field is set to anything else is 862's answer wearing rung 60's record - the strategy built, parked and documented, and never reached, so the press would return a log indistinguishable from rung 59's while every file said otherwise"
                fi
