                    layout_fail "st_media_memdev_info (at $mi_addr) stores its FIRST field (\`mi_mdev\`) from ${mi_st_dst}, and the nearest instruction above that store which writes ${mi_st_dst} is [${mi_mdev_set}]. $mi_why. **The check is anchored to the store's own register rather than to a constant anywhere in the body** ([[mi4-linked-code-order-is-not-source-order]]), because this body legitimately carries a \`#1\` (the \`mi_size\` floor, emitted as \`movweq rX, #1\`) and a pattern that scanned for one would refuse a correct build. Nothing is rebuilt by this refusal"
